{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And the woman saw.</b> In her heart." "<b>And the tree was desirable,</b> because she would grow wise and her eyes would be opened," "<b>and she gave to him with her,</b> for they ate it together and she revealed to him the secret of the serpent. Now Adam was not inadvertent, therefore he was punished. Many say that the Tree of Knowledge was a fig tree, because they found \"and they sewed fig leaves\" (Genesis 3:7). Had this been so, Scripture would have said \"and they sewed leaves of the Tree of Knowledge.\" Also, many said it was wheat. What seems correct to me is that the two trees are in the Garden of Eden and exist nowhere else on the face of the earth. One is the Tree of Knowledge, and it gives rise to the desire for intercourse; therefore the man and his wife covered their nakedness. The meaning of ויתפרו is known, as in \"I sewed sackcloth upon my skin\" (Job 16:15). Those who seek a needle are mistaken, for they use a fine tree [to do] their work [i.e. as a needle]. And when Adam ate from the Tree of Knowledge, he knew his wife, and this \"knowing\" is a euphemism for intercourse, and because of the Tree of Knowledge it is called thus. Also a youth, when he knows good and evil, then begins to desire intercourse." "<b>and the Tree of Life.</b> Which would add life and cause the man to live many years — the expression לעולם עד עולם ועד does not [necessarily mean eternity]; thus \"and he shall serve him forever (לעולם)\" (Exodus 21:6), \"and he dwelt there forever (עד עולם)\" (I Samuel 1:22), and many others. The commentators said regarding \"for on the day you eat of it you shall surely die,\" that he was not created on the pattern that he would die, but only when he sinned was death decreed upon him. Many ask: what was the sin of his offspring? These are words of wind. For the spirit of man and beast is one; by it he exists and perceives in this world, and the death of this [spirit] is like the death of that [beast], besides the supernal portion that man has in excess of beast. And one of the physicians of Greece has already brought complete proofs that it is impossible that human life should have no limit."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:08.804803493Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}